evelopments, SPA said. Fighting between Saudi Arabia and the Houthis has intensified since the group captured strategic areas along Yemen's Red Sea coast last month, advancing towards the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a key global shipping route for Gulf oil producers on the other side of the Arabian Peninsula from the Strait of Hormuz. The renewed conflict between the two sides has shattered a 2022 UN-brokered truce that largely halted attacks between the Saudi-led coalition, which backs Yemen's internationally recognised government, and the Houthis, who control the capital Sanaa. The Houthis have since stepped up attacks on Saudi airports, ports and oil facilities amid the wider US-Israeli war on Iran, while Saudi Arabia has responded with airstrikes against Houthi targets in Yemen. Riyadh has been repeatedly hit, including a deadly attack on King Khalid International Airport. Debris from an attempted strike also damaged a building belonging to oil giant Saudi Aramco in the capital. REUTERS", "stages_full": {"windows": {"windows": 9, "cap": 12, "pct_body_read": 100, "offsets_text": [[78, 267], [268, 485], [485, 726], [726, 972], [972, 1182], [1183, 1403], [1404, 1617], [1618, 1833], [1833, 1950]]}, "scan_dates": {"spots": {"attribution": 9, "date": 3, "entity": 45, "event": 12, "negation": 1}, "dates": [["Nov 19", "2026-11-19"], ["Thursday", "2026-11-19"], ["last month", "last month relative to 2026-11-19"]], "dates_resolved": 3, "anchor": "2026-11-19", "time_proxy": {"label": "time_proxy", "marker": "PROVISIONAL", "offset_days": [0, 0], "n": 2, "of": "resolved date minus published date, in days"}}, "facts": {"kinds": {"amount": 2, "date": 3, "name": 45, "triple": 27}, "stated": 39, "unbound": 38, "invalid": 0, "stated_amount": 2, "stated_date": 3, "quarantined": 0, "held": [], "items": [{"kind": "amount", "s": 904, "e": 907, "text": "two", "status": "stated"}, {"kind": "amount", "s": 1315, "e": 1318, "text": "two", "status": "stated"}, {"kind": "date", "s": 157, "e": 163